      "text": "Sept 15\u201316 FOMC... around 10 days out\n\nPersonally not interested in chasing swing longs up here. There have been some fantastic moves across the board and perhaps they continue, but a correction or two over the coming weeks wouldn't surprise me.\n\nOne thing I'm watching is the continued rotation in OI dominance as per previous occasions.\n\nBTC has been steadily losing share while \"Others\" has expanded considerably, now sitting roughly alongside BTC.\n\nDoesn't make it bearish in itself, but it does tell you where the speculative leverage has migrated.\n\nCombine that with some fairly thin moves on the way up and, for me, this is more a place to manage existing exposure than start forcing fresh swing longs.\n\nNo prediction, just recognising that the further leverage moves out the risk curve, the less attractive chasing becomes - and being more selective with trades - as is always the case.",
