      "text": "bitcoin:native \n\nPrice auctioned higher but ran into a decent wall of supply around the 365D rolling VWAP, with stacked sells sitting around the June & August swing highs / raneg highs. \n\nWas a decent move, but there was still a fair bit of sell-side to chew through if price wanted to continue higher.\n\nCurrent view is pretty simple, 50wma  & 365d rvwap are the key contextual levels for me here. \n\nIf price trades back below the 50w particularly then that\u2019s effectively 3 attempts, 3 rejections - and back below.\n\nI\u2019d be looking for a move into previous weeks vwap - rotate lower around 77-78s - should that hold then it becomes interesting again with it being a shallow consolidation - back below here then... I guess if its looks like a range and trades like one - then it probably is one...",
